      "side": 1,
      "message": "The `VM_GROWSDOWN` flag is only set on the main stack; pthread stacks don\u0027t have this flag. You can see that when looking at /proc/$pid/smaps and searching for entries with VmFlags containing \"gd\". So that doesn\u0027t give an indication of which way the stack grows.\n\nI think `CONFIG_STACK_GROWSUP` signals which way the stack grows on the current architecture (and that flag is only set on the parisc architecture). (I think Itanium was a weird exception with stacks growing _both_ directions and two stack pointers, or something like that, but that\u0027s gone from the upstream kernel now.)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 125,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 125,
        "endChar": 33
      },
